Z||000015||Formula88||08-20-2001||03:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by c m west:<BR><B>photoshop rendering of what will soon be on my notchback...<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/aussaysnooooo.jpg">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Looks like an old Datsun 240Z car front end that's been modded.  I think I like it. I like the old Z cars (pre-ZX).  I may even get one some day.  I don't care for the add-on wings, though.  They look too much like an afterthought.  But that's just my taste.  I like any mods to blend with the rest of the car.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fformula88||08-20-2001||05:13 PM||||The difference between a black Fiero GT and a Honda Civic with a big double-decker wing on the back?<P>The Fiero is a sports car, looked like a sports car before the wing and still looks like one after the wing.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">  Personally I don't think it looks bad in that picture, maybe a little big but not too bad)<P>The Honda Civic  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"> is a two door coupe version of a sedan platform  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">.  It is as conservatively styled as the 4 door version.  Putting a big huge double decker wing on it is as rediculous as bolting the same thing onto the back of a Chevy Lumina!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
